 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Differentiable Voxelization via Smoothed Winding Numbers](2325-differentiable-voxelization-via-smoothed-winding-numbers.md)
-Differentiable Voxelization via Smoothed Winding Numbers (DVX) is a method for voxelizing triangle meshes into smoothed winding number voxel grids that provides closed-form gradients with respect to mesh vertex positions, enabling gradient-based optimization of surface representations based on volumetric properties. Unlike [Differentiable Voxelization (MC/CF)](1742-differentiable-voxelization-mc-cf.md) which samples a non-smoothed winding number and uses automatic differentiation (yielding sparse near-surface derivative signals), this method yields a broader gradient pattern matching finite-difference references.
+Differentiable Voxelization via Smoothed Winding Numbers (DVX) is a method for voxelizing triangle meshes into smoothed winding number voxel grids that provides closed-form gradients with respect to mesh vertex positions, enabling gradient-based optimization of surface representations based on volumetric properties. Unlike [Differentiable Voxelization (MC/CF)](1742-differentiable-voxelization-mc-cf.md) which samples a non-smoothed winding number and uses automatic differentiation (yielding sparse near-surface derivative signals), this method yields a broader gradient pattern matching finite-difference references. Choose DVX when smooth volumetric gradients are required for optimization; choose MC/CF when sparse near-surface gradients or closed-form polygon splitting are preferred.
 
 ### [Differentiable Voxelization from Radiative Gaussians](2380-differentiable-voxelization-from-radiative-gaussians.md)
-This method provides a differentiable voxelizer $\mathcal{V}$ that efficiently queries a 3D density volume $V \in \mathbb{R}^{X \times Y \times Z}$ from a set of radiative Gaussians $G_3$. It solves the computational bottleneck of mapping continuous Gaussian splats to a discrete grid, enabling 3D regularization priors for tomographic reconstruction. Unlike [Differentiable Voxelization (MC/CF)](1742-differentiable-voxelization-mc-cf.md) which operates on polygonal meshes, this method operates directly on parametric Gaussian distributions, leveraging spatial tiling for acceleration.
+This method provides a differentiable voxelizer $\mathcal{V}$ that efficiently queries a 3D density volume $V \in \mathbb{R}^{X \times Y \times Z}$ from a set of radiative Gaussians $G_3$. It solves the computational bottleneck of mapping continuous Gaussian splats to a discrete grid, enabling 3D regularization priors for tomographic reconstruction. Unlike [Differentiable Voxelization (MC/CF)](1742-differentiable-voxelization-mc-cf.md) which operates on polygonal meshes, this method operates directly on parametric Gaussian distributions, leveraging spatial tiling for acceleration. Choose Radiative Gaussians for Gaussian splat rendering or tomographic priors; choose MC/CF for mesh-based differentiable rendering.
 
